# cairn transition journal — one PARTITION per checkout (phase 28, DJOUR-02).
#
# Two checkouts never write the same segment file, so a merge only ever has to
# concatenate. `union` is the built-in driver that does exactly that, and it is
# built-in on purpose: a CUSTOM driver needs a `merge.<name>.driver` entry in
# .git/config, and git NEVER clones config. A machine without that out-of-band
# setup step falls back to the default merge and conflicts with markers, in
# silence — measured in 28-RESEARCH.md, experiment E17. `union` also holds for
# rebase, cherry-pick and pull, measured in E15.
#
# What still needs this line even though partitions are disjoint: the SAME
# partition on two branches of the same checkout. Without `union` that is an
# add/add conflict (E8b). The reader folds each partition by
# (compacted_through_ts, then ts, nonce), so the concatenated blocks come back
# in the right order.
.cairn/journal/*.jsonl merge=union
